#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:67
#, no-c-format
msgid "Getting Started"
msgstr "Per començar"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:69
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is a short introduction to &kuser;. For more detailed information, see "
"<link linkend=\"using\">Usage</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:72
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Actually, you do not need to do anything to begin using &kuser; except <link "
"linkend=\"customizing\">configuration</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:75
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you have made the changes you want, you must <guimenuitem>Save</"
"guimenuitem> them for them to take effect. Either choose the Toolbar icon, "
"or use the <guimenu>File</guimenu> menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:82
#, no-c-format
msgid "Usage"
msgstr "Utilizacion"

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:85
#, no-c-format
msgid "Main Window"
msgstr "Fenèstra principala"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kuser; is a very simple application. In the main window you can see two "
"tabs: the list of users and the list of groups. To edit a user or a group, "
"just double click on it. The user or group properties dialog will appear."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:92
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>&kuser; Main Window</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>&kuser; Main Window</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid "User Properties Dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:108
#, no-c-format
msgid "The user properties dialog has various tabs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:110
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The number of tabs depends on the type of the user storage system and "
"whether quotas are being used. Additional tabs will appear if you have "
"shadow passwords, or any other similar things such as <filename>/etc/master."
"passwd</filename> in BSD flavor Unices."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:116
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>User Info</guilabel> Tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid "In the <guilabel>User Info</guilabel> tab you can modify:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:122
#, no-c-format
msgid "User Id"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:123
#, no-c-format
msgid "Full Name"
msgstr "Nom complet"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:124
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Login Shell</guilabel> (the list of login shells is taken from the "
"<filename>/etc/shells</filename> file)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:126
#, no-c-format
msgid "Home Folder"
msgstr "Repertòri personal"

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:127
#, no-c-format
msgid "Two office locations"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:128
#, no-c-format
msgid "Address"
msgstr "Adreça"

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid "Password"
msgstr "Mot de pas"

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:135
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Password Management</guilabel> Tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:137
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Password Management</guilabel> tab will appear if you have "
"shadow passwords, or any other similar things such as <filename>/etc/master."
"passwd</filename> in <acronym>BSD</acronym> flavor Unices."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:142
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>Extended Info</guilabel> tab you can modify parameters "
"related to extended account control:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:146
#, no-c-format
msgid "Minimum number of days between password changes"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:148
#, no-c-format
msgid "Number of days after which a password expires if it hasn't been changed"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:150
#, no-c-format
msgid "Number of days before expiration the user will be warned"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:152
#, no-c-format
msgid "Whether and when an account will be disabled if the password expires"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:154
#, no-c-format
msgid "A set date when the account expires"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:155
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Class</guilabel> (on <acronym>BSD</acronym> systems)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:158
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The date of the last password change is displayed near the top of the dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:165
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Quota</guilabel> Tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:167
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You will probably see the <guilabel>Quota</guilabel> tab only if you have at "
"least one mounted volume with quota enabled and a quota file present. There "
"you may modify all quota related parameters:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:172
#, no-c-format
msgid "File Soft Quota"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:173
#, no-c-format
msgid "File Hard Quota"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:174
#, no-c-format
msgid "File Time Limit (Grace Period)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:176
#, no-c-format
msgid "iNode Soft Quota"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:177
#, no-c-format
msgid "iNode Hard Quota"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:178
#, no-c-format
msgid "iNode Time Limit (Grace Period)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:182
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All these parameters can be changed for each file system that has user quota "
"enabled. File systems can be changed using the <guilabel>Quota Filesystem</"
"guilabel> box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:189
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Groups</guilabel> Tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:191
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Groups</guilabel> tab contains all the information about the "
"selected user's participation in groups. The primary group to which the user "
"belongs is set in the <guilabel>Primary Group</guilabel> box. The user can "
"be assigned to additional groups by checking them in the large box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:201
#, no-c-format
msgid "Group Properties"
msgstr "Propietats del grop"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:203
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Group Properties</guilabel> dialog contains a list of all "
"users. Check the boxes for each user to be assigned to the selected group."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:210
#, no-c-format
msgid "Adding, Editing and Deleting Users or Groups"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:212
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To add a user or group to the system, either choose <guimenuitem>Add</"
"guimenuitem> from the <guimenu>User</guimenu> or <guimenu>Group</guimenu> "
"menu, or click the relevant <guiicon>Add</guiicon> button on the toolbar. "
"The selected user or group can also be edited or deleted in the same way."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:222
#, no-c-format
msgid "Customizing &kuser;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:225
#, no-c-format
msgid "Edit user creation defaults"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:227
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To edit the user creation defaults you can use the <guilabel>Edit defaults</"
"guilabel> dialog, which is accessible via the menu "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Configure &kuser;</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice>. There you may change the defaults that are used "
"when creating a new user: Shell and Home Folder (or home folders volume). "
"You can choose whether to make a home folder on <quote>create</quote> or not,"
"and to copy a skeleton (standard configuration files) to the home folder or "
"not. You can also enable <guilabel>User Private Group</guilabel> mechanism, "
"which creates a new personal group with the creation of a new user, and "
"removes the personal group when the user is removed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:239
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The skeleton files for new users can be specified in the <guilabel>Sources </"
"guilabel> tab."
msgstr ""

